WEBVTT

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:25.910
All preparations for the division battle
qualifiers have been duly carried out.

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:27.700
I appreciate your efforts.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:30.950
According to reports, those four
we've been observing seem to have gained

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:35.250
the overwhelming popular support
of their respective divisions.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:38.290
As you have surmised, Prime Minister Tohoten,

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:41.790
in the unlikely event that
they collaborate once more,

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:45.750
they may one day pose
a threat to the Party of Words.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:48.540
That is why we have the division battle.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:55.080
If those four and the teams they lead
are defeated by others, that's just as well.

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:56.750
Even if they remain in the running,

00:00:56.750 --> 00:01:00.040
the four teams will compete against
each other in the final tournament,

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:03.660
which may prove to make the ruptures
among the four leaders conclusive.

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:07.330
The foolish men will defeat
each other in rap battles,

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:09.620
making the masses go wild with excitement.

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:12.080
In the meantime, we of the Party of Words

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:16.450
shall finish creating a
more stable organization.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:17.660
Yes, Prime Minister!

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:22.330
We apologize for the extended delay.

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:24.790
We of Chuohku hereby announce that

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:30.120
preparations to hold the division
battle qualifiers are now complete.

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:32.250
As your prime minister

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:34.700
and as head of the Party of Words,

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:37.700
I sincerely hope that the all-out rap
battles between the participating teams

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:42.410
will lead us all to new heights.

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:43.750
Rap!

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:45.120
Dance!

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:46.700
Scream!

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:49.080
Fighters from every division!

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:51.080
Use your hypnosis mics to hit your opponents

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:54.200
with every ounce of your strength and wisdom!

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:58.370
Now, let the division battle qualifiers begin!

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:35.450
Well, well, well! What an excellent view!

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:38.540
Ikebukuro's lookin' pretty cool from here!

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:41.370
Get down from there! It's not safe!

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:44.540
Tom, say something, will you?

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:46.250
What are you taking pictures of?

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:48.910
I've got to hand it to you, Japan.

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:51.040
Even your road work is cutting-edge.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:52.290
That's liquid nitrogen.

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:53.870
"Frozen Storage Tank"

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:53.870
That's liquid nitrogen.

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:54.160
"High-Pressure Gas"
"Avoid Collisions"

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:57.290
They're going to freeze the
water pipes and replace them.

00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:57.910
"High-Pressure Gas"
"Avoid Collisions"

00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:57.910
Tom, you sure do like signs
and lettering and stuff.

00:03:57.910 --> 00:03:59.790
"Freezing in Progress"
"Under Construction" "Safety First"

00:03:57.910 --> 00:03:59.790
Tom, you sure do like signs
and lettering and stuff.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:03.700
Graffiti is also an important
part of street culture, you know.

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:05.250
It certainly is.

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:06.580
But more importantly,

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:09.330
the division battle qualifiers have begun.

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:11.370
Oh, really?

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:14.080
At the qualifiers,
teams are divided into four blocks

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:17.040
and will compete at a specially-prepared venue.

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:19.830
There is a total of 32 participating teams.

00:04:19.830 --> 00:04:23.040
So, that means eight teams per block.

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:26.620
In particular, these four teams
are the ones to watch.

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:29.700
Ikebukuro's Buster Bros!!!,

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:32.250
Shinjuku's Matenro,

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:35.080
Shibuya's Fling Posse,

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:38.120
and Yokohama's MAD TRIGGER CREW.

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:42.660
These four teams just happen
to be scattered among the four blocks.

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:45.620
I get the feeling someone did that on purpose.

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:48.540
While Ichiro Yamada,
the leader of Buster Bros!!!,

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:51.450
has since reformed for the
sake of his younger brothers,

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:53.580
he was originally
a notorious juvenile delinquent.

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:56.080
His powerful flow and rhymes
are a force to be reckoned with.

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:59.120
The other members are
his younger brothers Jiro and Saburo.

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:01.580
They may be young, but they show promise.

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:05.250
It's a team with the kind of solidarity
that you would expect from brothers.

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:10.830
Matenro's leader Jakurai Jinguji
is a highly-gifted and skilled physician.

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:13.080
"Surgery in Progress"

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:13.080
Matenro's leader Jakurai Jinguji
is a highly-gifted and skilled physician.

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:14.870
"Surgery in Progress"

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:14.870
His characteristically cool lyrics and flow

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:17.830
are what you would expect
from a man with such a brilliant mind.

00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:22.870
The other members are Hifumi Izanami,
Shinjuku's number one host,

00:05:22.870 --> 00:05:26.750
and Doppo Kannonzaka, a salesman
for a medical equipment manufacturer.

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:29.120
As you would expect from
a professional in his field,

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:32.250
Hifumi's an expert at getting
the audience into the groove with his raps.

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:35.830
And Doppo fires off his
unique brand of tweet-like lyrics.

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:38.080
It's a team with a lot of variety.

00:05:39.790 --> 00:05:42.580
A host and an office worker, huh?

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:45.330
Next, we have Fling Posse's leader

00:05:45.330 --> 00:05:48.080
Ramuda Amemura, a hot fashion designer.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:51.660
He raps as though
he were showing you an illusion.

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:54.540
The other members are
the popular novelist Gentaro Yumeno,

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:57.830
whose poetic and
narrative lyrics are his trademark,

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:00.700
and the wandering gambler Dice Arisugawa,

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:04.580
whose thrilling raps are what you would
expect from a man who bets on anything.

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:08.620
It's a team of free spirits who
aren't bound by society's shackles.

00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:11.370
These two have no sense of unity.

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:14.750
It's pretty hard to imagine
what kind of raps they'll do.

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:20.080
Last, we have the leader of Yokohama's
MAD TRIGGER CREW, Samatoki Aohitsugi.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:22.000
He's the <i>wakagashira </i>of a Yakuza syndicate.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:25.500
His explosive and sensational
raps are his selling point.

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:28.370
Police officer Jyuto Iruma
is one of the other members.

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:30.700
While rumor has it that he's a dirty cop,

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:34.330
one can glimpse a kind of
justice hidden within his raps.

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:36.500
There may be some sort of reason behind this.

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:40.950
And then there's Rio Mason Busujima,
ex-special forces in the military.

00:06:40.950 --> 00:06:42.200
As you would expect from a serviceman,

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:44.830
he has the fearlessness
to attack his enemies head-on

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:47.160
and rout any of them who stand in his way.

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:49.700
A yakuza, a police officer,
and a serviceman, huh?

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:51.790
What a fearsome combination!

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:54.620
They're the mad dog living within the system.

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:57.250
Mad dog? More like a mutt, I'd say.

00:06:57.250 --> 00:06:59.750
You've been making these smart-assed
remarks this entire time.

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:01.660
It's just the age I'm at right now.

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:03.410
People say that about others, not themselves!

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:08.450
All of these guys are
forces to be reckoned with.

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:10.370
The leaders of these four teams

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:14.910
used to be members of a team called
The Dirty Dawg, but it broke up.

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:15.910
Why?

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:17.000
I'm not sure.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:19.790
There must be some explanation.

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:23.830
But still, things have started
to get interesting, haven't they?

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:32.620
There's nothing better
than fishing on a calm day like today.

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:34.660
If only this peaceful time would last forever...

00:07:34.660 --> 00:07:36.450
Dr. Jinguji!

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:39.040
I thought I'd find you here!

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:41.330
Why, hello you two.
What seems to be the trouble?

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:43.540
Dr. Jinguji, have you heard?

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:46.910
The qualifiers for the
division battle have finally begun.

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:51.330
Oh, really? So, the decisive
battle has begun at last.

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:53.790
I'm so stoked!

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:55.910
I'm actually kind of nervous...

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:57.660
What do you mean?

00:07:57.660 --> 00:07:59.870
The good doctor and I have got your back!

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:01.620
Relax, Doppomine!

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:03.160
--Whoa, whoaaaa!
--Doppo!

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:04.370
Doppomine! Uwahh!

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:07.000
Don't drag me down with you!

00:08:09.370 --> 00:08:11.410
The qualifiers will begin at last.

00:08:11.410 --> 00:08:13.290
The blocks have been divided so that

00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:15.620
the four teams will face
each other in the finals.

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:17.250
You will give us some results

00:08:17.250 --> 00:08:19.580
by making it through the qualifiers
and defeating the other three leaders.

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:22.660
Results? I've already given you some results.

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:25.830
Who do you think was the guy
behind The Dirty Dawg's break-up?

00:08:25.830 --> 00:08:28.410
That's ancient history.

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:31.290
What we want are some new results.

00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:33.250
Make it through the qualifiers.

00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:35.450
We expect you to deliver.

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:43.660
What was that all about?

00:08:45.160 --> 00:08:48.200
They're up to something.

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:49.410
<i>Who </i>are they?

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:51.080
And <i>what </i>are they up to?

00:08:51.080 --> 00:08:52.910
Oh my gosh! How long have you been there?!

00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:54.290
We just got here a second ago.

00:08:54.290 --> 00:08:55.620
The qualifiers have begun, man.

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:57.080
I know, I know!

00:08:57.080 --> 00:08:59.500
All right then, let me tell you my plan!

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:02.200
Let's all go out and eat something fancy today!

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:04.450
No shit, man? Free food?

00:09:04.450 --> 00:09:09.620
I need you both to do a lot of work
for the team from now on, you see.

00:09:11.330 --> 00:09:16.370
It appears the time has finally come for us
to make our presence known to Chuohku.

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:18.040
Time to commence our plan of operations.

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:20.750
Plan of operations?
We have a plan of operations?

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:22.160
Fuck yeah!

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:26.160
We'll crush any asshole who dares
to oppose us and show 'em no mercy!

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:28.290
You can't call that a plan of operations.

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:30.660
Hmph. All right then.

00:09:30.660 --> 00:09:34.080
We'll include Jyuto and come up
with a slightly better plan of operations.

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:35.040
"Traffic Safety Campaign in Effect"

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:36.040
All right.

00:09:36.040 --> 00:09:36.500
"Schedule"

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:37.870
I'm on my way.

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:41.040
I'm stepping out for a moment.

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:46.580
That bastard Iruma's been
getting pretty cocky these days.

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:49.040
All on account of MAD TRIGGER CREW.

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:52.120
It's not wise for a police officer
to associate with the yakuza.

00:09:52.120 --> 00:09:55.370
It's a question of compliance.

00:09:55.370 --> 00:09:59.910
This is a great opportunity
to take Iruma down a notch or two.

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:00.290
"Yorozuya Yamada"

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:00.290
This is a great opportunity
to take Iruma down a notch or two.

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:02.870
"Yorozuya Yamada"

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:02.870
Found the cat you were looking for.

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:05.040
"Yorozuya Yamada"

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:05.040
Also found the wallet like you asked.

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:07.500
Thanks, guys. You're real lifesavers!

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:11.700
No prob! Buster Bros!!!
is our pride and joy, you know.

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:14.080
If it helps you guys
concentrate on the qualifiers,

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:16.370
doing stuff like this is no sweat.

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:18.370
"Saburo"

00:10:20.450 --> 00:10:22.660
Jiro, you making any progress?

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:24.160
I sure am!

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:26.330
I already completed three of the tasks.

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:28.540
I'm finished with five, myself.

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:31.330
All you've been doing is sitting
in front of a computer, right?

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:34.450
Since you live in the Stone Age,
Jiro, you may not know this,

00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:37.290
but lots of things can be done using a computer.

00:10:37.290 --> 00:10:39.750
Tsk. So, how's Big Bro coming along?

00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:41.410
Seems he's having some trouble.

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:44.620
Brother Ichi's dealing
with a real criminal, you know.

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:48.700
Huh?! What's up with these posts?

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.450
Hey, you! Stop!

00:10:55.450 --> 00:10:57.160
Shut the fuck up, man!

00:10:57.160 --> 00:10:59.160
--Outta my way, asshole!
--Stop!

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:02.160
Huh?!

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:03.160
Damn!

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:04.660
What the fuck?!

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:05.830
Uwahhh!

00:11:07.370 --> 00:11:09.000
God damn it!

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:16.580
Ichiro! Don't think you can keep on actin'
like a big shot for as long as you want!

00:11:16.580 --> 00:11:19.620
Now you won't be able
to take part in the division battle!

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:20.750
What are you talking about?

00:11:20.750 --> 00:11:23.620
Both you and the division battle are done for!

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:26.830
An hour from now, everything goes <i>ka-boom</i>!

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:28.910
--Get in the car!
--God damn it!

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:31.160
"Takoyaki"

00:11:31.160 --> 00:11:33.450
Apparently, the guy's a rapper from Saitama.

00:11:33.450 --> 00:11:36.250
"Takoyaki"

00:11:33.450 --> 00:11:36.250
But he's also a punk that's repeatedly
stirred up trouble at shopping arcades.

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:39.120
With your help I was able to nab him.

00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:40.620
You have my thanks.

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:43.250
I was only taking photos
of your accomplishments.

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:45.160
Are you a photographer?

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:48.950
Yeah, I follow street
culture all over the world.

00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:51.410
I took some photos of your
accomplishments the other day as well.

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:53.910
Say, you wouldn't happen to be the guy
who did that article on us a while back?

00:11:53.910 --> 00:11:54.660
"Buster Bros!!! Resolve Hostage Situation"

00:11:53.910 --> 00:11:54.660
Say, you wouldn't happen to be the guy
who did that article on us a while back?

00:11:54.660 --> 00:11:57.830
"Buster Bros!!! Resolve Hostage Situation"

00:11:54.660 --> 00:11:57.830
That made for some good publicity
and has been a boon for our business as well.

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:01.040
These're piping hot...

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:01.500
"Takoyaki 450 Yen"

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:04.160
Must be amazing to travel all over the world.

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:06.160
"Takoyaki 450 Yen"

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:06.160
As soon as my kid brothers
start living on their own,

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:08.500
I wouldn't mind leading
that kind of life myself.

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:10.660
I know about your background.

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:12.540
I'm in a similar situation myself.

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:14.790
I have two others to take care of.

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:16.700
Really? Are they your siblings?

00:12:16.700 --> 00:12:17.620
They're not related to me,

00:12:17.620 --> 00:12:20.540
but I think they would've headed down
the wrong path if I hadn't stepped in.

00:12:20.540 --> 00:12:22.450
I've got them working as my assistants.

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:24.540
That's even more amazing.

00:12:25.620 --> 00:12:29.120
Considering you're so young,
you're the one who's amazing, Ichiro.

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:30.700
I'm Tom.

00:12:33.790 --> 00:12:36.750
So, tell me, are you guys worried
about the division battle?

00:12:36.750 --> 00:12:39.500
Nope, now that our work is done,

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:41.910
we can rest easy and
devote ourselves to the qualifiers.

00:12:41.910 --> 00:12:44.540
You're one of the teams
in the spotlight and all.

00:12:44.540 --> 00:12:46.250
So, I figure that your team

00:12:46.250 --> 00:12:50.200
and the three others fronted by ex-Dirty Dawg
members will make it to the finals.

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:51.750
I see...

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:56.700
Who's that guy talking with Big Bro?

00:12:56.700 --> 00:12:59.120
This may be none of my business,

00:12:59.120 --> 00:13:01.580
but why did The Dirty Dawg break up?

00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:07.200
It's hard to sum up
what happened to The Dirty Dawg.

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:13.290
At the time, there was a
plot involving Jiro and Saburo,

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:17.080
which caused a rift to form
between me and Samatoki.

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:22.120
Samatoki and I both know perfectly
well that Chuohku was behind it.

00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:26.200
But even so, I've got to settle
the score with Samatoki.

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:29.160
Any trouble that arises during a
rap battle must be settled by a rap battle.

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:31.410
That's how I operate.

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:33.580
I'll make it through
the qualifiers no matter what.

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:36.700
Not just for me,
but for Jiro and Saburo as well.

00:13:36.700 --> 00:13:38.000
Big Bro...

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:39.580
Brother Ichi...

00:13:39.580 --> 00:13:41.660
And you're determined to do that...

00:13:41.660 --> 00:13:43.080
Yeah...

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:45.410
Huh? Jiro and Saburo, what's up?

00:13:45.410 --> 00:13:48.500
Big Bro, we tried calling you,
but you wouldn't pick up.

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:49.870
Sorry about that.

00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:51.910
I kind of had my hands full.

00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:53.950
Uh, who's this?

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:55.450
This is Tom.

00:13:55.450 --> 00:13:58.540
He's the photographer who took the
photo of us we saw on the web a while back.

00:13:58.540 --> 00:14:01.000
Wow, a photographer? That's awesome!

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:02.620
So, it was him...

00:14:02.620 --> 00:14:05.410
Nice to meet you, Jiro and Saburo.

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:07.580
So, what's up, you two?

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:08.870
Oh, right!

00:14:08.870 --> 00:14:11.450
Actually, Brother Ichi,
we saw some guys chatting

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:14.750
on an underground message board
about shutting down the division battle.

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:16.750
Shutting down the division battle?

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:19.200
They mentioned the Toyotama Line or something.

00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:21.540
Is that where they're
planning to stir things up?

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:24.000
But I've never heard of such
a train line, have you?

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:25.660
I couldn't find it on the web, either.

00:14:25.660 --> 00:14:27.450
So, it's bogus then, don't you think?

00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:30.120
Don't you have any other leads?

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:31.580
That's why we're here.

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:34.410
It seems as though the guy you were
chasing is one of them, Brother Ichi.

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:36.540
If we ask him, we might learn something.

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:39.580
I already turned him over to the police.

00:14:39.580 --> 00:14:41.950
But now that you mention it...

00:14:41.950 --> 00:14:44.790
Both you and the division battle are done for!

00:14:44.790 --> 00:14:48.620
An hour from now, everything goes <i>ka-boom</i>!

00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:52.120
<i>Ka-boom</i>?! Could he be talking about a bomb?

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:54.370
But where did they plant it?

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:57.830
Hey! Why don't we call the cops and ask the guy?

00:14:57.830 --> 00:15:00.410
It's going to go off in an hour.
We haven't got the time.

00:15:00.410 --> 00:15:02.120
If he stonewalls us, it's over.

00:15:02.120 --> 00:15:04.540
So, where do we look?

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:07.330
If they want to shut down the division battle...

00:15:07.330 --> 00:15:09.290
it may be at the venue!

00:15:09.290 --> 00:15:10.870
Jiro! Saburo! Let's go!

00:15:10.870 --> 00:15:12.250
--Yeah!
--OK!

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:19.330
It's around here somewhere...

00:15:19.330 --> 00:15:22.040
Well, well, if it isn't the Buster Bros!!!

00:15:22.870 --> 00:15:25.950
Sadamezuka of the Tenderloins, if memory serves.

00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:28.950
What are you doing here?
Come to mess with us again?

00:15:28.950 --> 00:15:31.080
It pains me to say this, Ichiro Yamada,

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:35.660
but your raps have resonated
throughout this old soul of mine:

00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:37.950
from Kita-Senju in the north
to Kamata in the south!

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:39.830
"Senju Honcho Shopping Street"

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:39.830
from Kita-Senju in the north
to Kamata in the south!

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:42.750
"Kamata Onsen"

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:42.750
from Kita-Senju in the north
to Kamata in the south!

00:15:42.910 --> 00:15:44.910
That's a pretty small soul you've got there...

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:46.540
I've taken a shine to you, kid!

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:49.540
You guys have got my support!

00:15:49.540 --> 00:15:52.250
Brother Ichi, they may be just the help we need.

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:55.620
If that's the case, then before you back us,
help us look for something.

00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:57.540
We'll give you whatever help you need!

00:15:57.540 --> 00:16:00.080
So, what are we looking for?

00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:02.500
Well, we think it's somewhere
around this venue...

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:03.160
A bomb.

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:05.700
Huh?! A... bomb...?!

00:16:05.700 --> 00:16:08.080
Aren't you setting the bar a little high?

00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:10.160
Quit whining and go look for it!

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:12.290
Yessir!

00:16:12.290 --> 00:16:13.410
Let's look for it, too!

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:14.700
--Yeah!
--OK!

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:24.040
Tom, this is an emergency.
What do you expect to achieve by coming here?

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:26.330
We've also got to head over to the venue.

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:31.790
Hmm, even if there is a bomb,
it may not be at the venue, you know.

00:16:31.790 --> 00:16:34.790
That phrase has been bugging me:
"Toyotama Line."

00:16:34.790 --> 00:16:36.750
I hear you, man.

00:16:36.750 --> 00:16:40.290
Rulers always settle themselves in
their lofty perches in order to contemplate.

00:16:40.290 --> 00:16:41.950
You be quiet!

00:16:41.950 --> 00:16:44.080
No, he's actually got a point.

00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:48.790
When I get lost, I'm the type that goes up
somewhere high to get a bird's-eye view.

00:16:48.790 --> 00:16:51.370
Line, hmm...

00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:56.290
It's not a train line, but I've seen something
with that name somewhere before.

00:16:57.410 --> 00:17:00.160
Iris, pull up my photos.

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:02.790
"Ikebukuro Nishiguchi Park"

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:07.660
Any luck?

00:17:07.660 --> 00:17:09.120
Nope, Big Bro.

00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:11.120
Me neither.

00:17:11.120 --> 00:17:12.870
Damn...

00:17:12.870 --> 00:17:13.950
"Tom"

00:17:13.950 --> 00:17:16.910
Ichiro, I've figured out
what the Toyotama Line is.

00:17:16.910 --> 00:17:18.160
Really?!

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:20.290
It's the name of a power line.

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:20.370
But the Toyotama Line goes
underground near Loop Road No. 7.

00:17:20.370 --> 00:17:24.160
"Toyotama Line"

00:17:20.370 --> 00:17:24.160
But the Toyotama Line goes
underground near Loop Road No. 7.

00:17:24.160 --> 00:17:26.790
That's because the power lines
in the center of Tokyo are all buried.

00:17:26.790 --> 00:17:29.330
So, did they plant it there?

00:17:29.330 --> 00:17:32.700
That reminds me, there's
an electrical substation in Ikebukuro.

00:17:32.700 --> 00:17:34.870
That might be what they're after.

00:17:34.870 --> 00:17:36.450
A blackout in Ikebukuro!

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:38.040
That would be a big deal!

00:17:38.040 --> 00:17:40.410
If something like that happened,
it would wreak havoc with

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:43.620
traffic signals and medical care,
not to mention the qualifiers.

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:45.160
To the electrical substation! On the double!

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:46.000
--Yeah!
--OK!

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:47.620
We'd better hurry, too.

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:48.950
To the electrical substation, right?

00:17:48.950 --> 00:17:51.540
No. There's another place
we need to go to first.

00:17:51.540 --> 00:17:52.750
Huh?

00:17:56.290 --> 00:17:57.450
Big Bro!

00:17:58.660 --> 00:18:00.370
This has got to be the place.

00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:01.700
Let's move!

00:18:13.370 --> 00:18:15.120
Buster Bros!!!

00:18:15.120 --> 00:18:17.450
Ichiro Yamada! How did you find this place?

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:20.200
We know all about your evil schemes!

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:22.040
Who the hell are you guys?

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:24.370
We're a team of rappers from Saitama!

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:27.000
The Electric DynaMonks!

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:31.200
Hey, do the words "Electric Dynamo"
and "Monks" even rhyme?

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:32.790
It's just a stupid play on words.

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:34.580
Why the hell are you doing this?

00:18:34.580 --> 00:18:39.160
We'll do anything to keep the
Buster Bros!!! from going to the finals!

00:18:39.160 --> 00:18:44.330
It's 'cause of you guys that people
mock us and say we can't cross the border!

00:18:44.330 --> 00:18:46.370
I didn't know Saitama was a foreign country...

00:18:46.370 --> 00:18:50.040
Our electrifying rhymes'll whack you hard!

00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:51.290
And their "rhymes're wack, you hear?"

00:18:51.290 --> 00:18:53.290
Oh, enough with the snide remarks!

00:18:53.290 --> 00:18:54.910
Here we go!

00:18:54.910 --> 00:18:56.200
There's no time to waste!

00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:57.290
Let's rip these guys a new one!

00:18:57.290 --> 00:18:59.000
Jiro! Saburo!

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:00.330
--Yeah!
--OK!

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:08.790
♬ 3, 2, 1. Let's go ♬

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:11.870
♬ Countdown, time for judgment,
we'll give you to the count of 3 ♬

00:19:11.870 --> 00:19:13.160
--♬ Out of the way ♬
--♬ aight? ♬

00:19:13.160 --> 00:19:16.290
♬ Generator, accelerator,
my mic cord's a sparkin' fuse ♬

00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:17.410
♬ It's all over for you ♬

00:19:17.410 --> 00:19:19.370
♬ No time to deal with small fry ♬

00:19:19.370 --> 00:19:21.160
♬ Laugh while you can ♬

00:19:21.160 --> 00:19:22.450
--♬ Count, Three ♬
--♬ Two ♬
--♬ One ♬

00:19:22.450 --> 00:19:23.370
♬ These heavy hitting punches are gonna hit ♬

00:19:23.370 --> 00:19:24.290
♬ Yamada Bros ♬

00:19:24.290 --> 00:19:26.580
--♬ Pass the mic ♬
--♬ Hit it ♬

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:29.120
♬ Ignited like putting fire to a fuse ♬

00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:31.330
♬ Y'all three seconds away from going boom ♬

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:33.450
♬ Something smells, don't try baring your teeth ♬

00:19:33.450 --> 00:19:34.040
♬ Cuz your efforts are weak ♬

00:19:34.040 --> 00:19:34.870
♬ This love for our hometown in me ♬

00:19:34.870 --> 00:19:35.700
♬ is like TNT ♬

00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:37.620
♬ Your skills are out of order ♬

00:19:37.620 --> 00:19:38.910
♬ You can't cross this checkpoint ♬

00:19:38.910 --> 00:19:40.330
♬ let alone the country border ♬

00:19:40.330 --> 00:19:41.660
♬ I'm the best, you're the rest ♬

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:43.200
♬ In a three-second take over ♬

00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:44.700
♬ Game over ♬

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:46.200
♬ Let's go ♬

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:50.790
♬ Countdown, it's time, not a second to lose,
get outta my sight! Aight? ♬

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:52.660
♬ Dropping a rhyme bomb, fire in the hole ♬

00:19:52.660 --> 00:19:53.450
♬ Buster Bros!!! ♬

00:19:53.450 --> 00:19:54.870
♬ This flow is out of control ♬

00:19:54.870 --> 00:19:56.620
♬ Unstoppable hands on a clock ♬

00:19:56.620 --> 00:19:58.750
♬ Hurry if you don't wanna be
beaten on your own block ♬

00:19:58.750 --> 00:20:00.000
--♬ Count, Three ♬
--♬ Two ♬
--♬ One ♬

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:00.870
♬ We are BUSTER ♬

00:20:00.870 --> 00:20:01.830
♬ It's past the deadline ♬

00:20:01.830 --> 00:20:02.540
♬ Too bad ♬

00:20:02.540 --> 00:20:04.250
♬ You're outta time ♬

00:20:10.290 --> 00:20:13.040
But you guys are too late...

00:20:13.040 --> 00:20:15.620
Pretty soon it'll all go <i>ka-boom</i>...

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:27.160
Hey, what've we got here?

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:29.370
What does it look like? It's a bomb, you idiot!

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:31.040
I knew that!

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:33.500
It's just that we've got
less than a minute left!

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:34.160
Brother Ichi!

00:20:34.160 --> 00:20:35.830
Big Bro! What are you doing?

00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:38.660
I've got to get this as far away
from here as possible!

00:20:44.950 --> 00:20:46.700
"High-Pressure Gas"

00:20:47.540 --> 00:20:48.870
What the--?!

00:20:51.410 --> 00:20:53.660
--Tom!
--Toss it to me, Ichiro!

00:20:53.660 --> 00:20:56.040
Eyarghhhhhh!

00:21:01.200 --> 00:21:03.370
Rex!

00:21:03.370 --> 00:21:05.200
Touchdown!

00:21:11.330 --> 00:21:13.120
A minute has passed...

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:16.580
It hasn't gone off. What's the deal?

00:21:19.330 --> 00:21:21.450
That's liquid nitrogen.

00:21:21.450 --> 00:21:24.660
When you put a battery-powered
bomb in liquid nitrogen,

00:21:24.660 --> 00:21:26.950
the battery freezes,
which keeps the bomb from going off.

00:21:26.950 --> 00:21:28.250
Wow, really?

00:21:28.250 --> 00:21:30.660
But where did you get it from?

00:21:31.450 --> 00:21:34.040
I "borrowed" it from a construction site.

00:21:34.040 --> 00:21:36.120
Aw, c'mon! This place
has turned into a madhouse!

00:21:36.120 --> 00:21:40.410
Like we had a choice! We had
to save the division battle, you know.

00:21:40.410 --> 00:21:45.580
Exactly. It'd be pretty dull if we'd lost
Buster Bros!!! to something like this.

00:21:45.580 --> 00:21:48.910
All right, we'd better go tell
the authorities what happened.

00:21:48.910 --> 00:21:52.790
You guys are some crazy bastards.

00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:55.000
That makes two of us!

00:21:59.870 --> 00:22:04.330
We will now commence Round 1
for the Division Battle Qualifiers Block A!

00:22:04.330 --> 00:22:08.120
The first team up is Ikebukuro's Buster Bros!!!

00:22:08.120 --> 00:22:10.500
These are the qualifiers
we fought hard to protect!

00:22:10.500 --> 00:22:12.290
Let's show 'em what we're made of!

00:22:12.290 --> 00:22:14.790
Buster Bros!!! will sock it to 'em!

00:22:14.790 --> 00:22:16.870
Hell yeah!
